    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We describe the IRMA framework for supervisory control of complex, distributed production processes and describe an application of this framework to emissions control and troubleshooting for geothermal power plants. We describe Gaussian influence diagrams, the mathematical formalism upon which our control regime is based, and we show how the Schemer multiprocessing architecture supports a demonstration of applicability of our controller and diagnostician to the plant by supporting execution of a simulation model of the plant and integrating them with it.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Johnson, Eric R. and Fehling, Michael R. and Poland, William B.. (1993). TR089: IRMA: A Supervisory Control Architecture for Production Control. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/dy400mc7073",
